              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Latin for the chin, then the Latin for the back."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: cubitum, cubitī",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "cubitum, cubitī — \"an elbow\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "cubitum is built on cubō, \"to lie down, to recline\" (EtymDB 2.1): the elbow is what one leans on at table. English cubit, the length from elbow to fingertip, comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
